WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.236
-When did you realize that
you have perfect pitch?

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.337
-Right.
-Do you know this?

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:05.838
Do you know what that is?
Perfect pitch?

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.641
Less than 1% of us have
this talent, but basically --

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.109
-I think you might have it.

00:00:10.109 --> 00:00:12.545
The Roots told me you might
low-key have it.

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.113
-Oh, I don't think I have it.

00:00:14.113 --> 00:00:16.615
-It means you can like, hear,
like, any note.

00:00:16.615 --> 00:00:19.886
Like, if I were to tell you to
play an F sharp, it would be --

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:23.523
[ Vocalizes note ]

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.624
-Wow.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.326
-Or a G.
[ Vocalizes note ]

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:30.062
Or C sharp.
[ Vocalizes note ]

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:32.064
-What if I gave you,
like, B flat?

00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:34.833
-[ Vocalizes note ]

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:36.235
-Is that right?

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.438
-So, it's almost like I
memorized the notes in my head,

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:41.207
and I could do it from
when I was like four years old.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.142
It's like a weird --
It's a very odd thing.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:44.544
-That's unbelievable.
-Yeah.

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.379
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:51.017
-Yeah, it definitely affects me
socially sometimes

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:54.120
because I was in a hotel room
the other night,

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.323
and usually when you hear
car horns and fire alarms,

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.525
they're at minor
second intervals, like...

00:00:59.525 --> 00:01:01.360
[ Vocalizes notes ]

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.763
Like, "Jaws" is like, "Get out
of the water," Jaws.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.698
[ Vocalizes "Jaws" theme ]

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.133
And that's what
a fire alarm is sometimes,

00:01:08.133 --> 00:01:10.236
and it's two notes rubbing
against each other,

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.539
and it tells you to get the hell
out the building,

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:14.607
and I was on the 11th floor,

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:15.975
and I wasn't getting
out of the building.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.677
I was, like, rearranging notes
in my my mind,

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:18.978
and I was like,
"What if it was like..."

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:20.613
[ Vocalizes notes ]

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.414
Like, there was one time --

00:01:22.414 --> 00:01:23.883
-You're harmonizing with
the alarm?

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.451
-I'm harmonizing with the alarm.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.587
I let my entire school out early
one time

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.223
because there was a digital bell
that went like this.

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:32.257
Rumson-Fair Haven Regional
High School.

00:01:32.257 --> 00:01:33.526
I got suspended for this.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:36.462
It went...
[ Mimics bell ]

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:39.298
So, I was -- I wanted --
It was almost summer break,

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:41.801
and I went into the middle of
the hall and went into

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:44.403
a very reverberant part of
the school and just went...

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:46.138
[ Mimics bell ]

00:01:46.138 --> 00:01:48.441
I let the entire school out
early.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.275
-No way!

00:01:50.275 --> 00:01:51.644
That's awesome!

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.447
-I got suspended for that.
That was not good.

